WEBVTT

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.690
Is this Kiroranke Nispa?

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.860
These Russian border guards 
were after Kiro-chan.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.120
What's he doing on a wanted poster?

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.810
When I was 15...

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.710
I met a group of anti-government 
extremists in St. Petersburg.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:01.540
Aca...

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.190
Wilk!

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.680
Asirpa's father was there, as well.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.690
We killed the Emperor of Russia.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:47.770
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:59.510
<b>Episode Thirty
Bad Sign</b>

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.510
<i>I've been watching him for an hour,</i>

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.630
<i>and not only has he not moved, 
I can't even see him breathing.</i>

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.420
<i>And now that I look closer,</i>

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.060
<i>the way he's hiding is clumsy.</i>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.530
<i>You can see his gun and 
his body even from below.</i>

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:20.580
<i>A man capable of firing that shot 
wouldn't make a mistake like that.</i>

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.710
<i>It was only a single shot, but it was 
clearly a shot from an experienced sniper.</i>

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.040
<i>I'll keep watching him as I move.</i>

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.280
He's late.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.860
Should we go help Ogata-chan?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.450
No, he said he'd go alone.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.380
We shouldn't get between them. It's not safe.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:54.280
Let's believe in his skills 
and wait for him to finish.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.960
<i>That's...</i>

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.620
<i>I couldn't tell without the sunlight.</i>

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.370
<i>He covered his tracks in the snow?</i>

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.200
<i>Where do they lead?</i>

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:56.900
<i>A Uilta coffin!</i>

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.360
<i>That's why he's not moving! It's a decoy!</i>

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.690
Ogata's come back.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.000
You ain't looking so good.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.720
Not that you ever do.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.540
You've got a terrible fever.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.780
I just put a little too 
much snow in my mouth.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.380
It's nothing.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.080
<i>Why not have some hot water?</i>

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.390
<i>You should drink a lot.</i>

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.350
We're getting out of here.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.060
<i>Aren't you cold, Brother?</i>

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:29.670
I'm so happy you invited me along.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.530
It feels like they're 
avoiding me at the barracks.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:38.540
Yuusaku-dono, will you come 
to another bar with me?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.070
Yes, of course.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.990
There's an old myth about how virgin 
girls can't be hit by bullets,

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.560
so people would carry locks of their 
pubic hair as a good luck charm.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.430
And male virgins began to 
be treated the same way.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:07:01.150
A handsome countenance, 
proper manners, good grades in training...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.980
The flag-bearer is the 
regiment's face, in a way.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.790
I've heard that part of the reason 
you were chosen for flag-bearer

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.530
is that you've never known a woman.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:14.640
The flag-bearer is the 
first into the enemy ranks,

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.800
so they have the highest death 
rate of any job in the army.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.100
The women at this brothel are tight-lipped.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.500
Yuusaku-dono,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.610
all that matters is that the 
regiment believes you're a virgin.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:35.620
Brothers get into trouble together, don't they?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.320
Brother...

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.610
I'm sorry.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:53.350
Send Yuusaku-dono out from the back.
 Don't let him be seen.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.370
That's his cousin's home, supposedly.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:04.630
Can you stand?

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.790
Let's get him inside and warmed up.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:20.770
This is suwashi. It's a branch 
whose name means "bitter bush."

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.520
The Ainu boil it and then drink 
the water when they get a cold.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.480
Put this on over you.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.170
Let the steam hit you, 
and sweat as much as possible.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:32.600
It's a method of healing called yaysumawkare.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:36.540
What?

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:47.150
The cousin is a sama. The sama are those 
who mediate between man and the gods.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.670
They pray to heal the sick.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:02.680
They believe that the sick are 
possessed by demons named amba.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.930
Through singing and drums, they communicate 
with the gods to have them driven away.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:11.740
The louder the noise, 
the faster the gods will come.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.070
Just stop...

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:27.960
Music is a spiritual thing with a 
strong effect on the subconscious.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.420
It makes clear the connection 
between the patient,

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.970
and whatever wicked thing haunts them.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.020
Lieutenant Tsurumi...

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.650
That'll be all.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.750
I have an important matter to 
discuss with the lieutenant.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:03.740
Your brother's every bit 
the man they say he is.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.870
I believe he simply got scared.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.330
I hope so.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.170
I'll win him over.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:20.750
If he's got a strong sense of justice, 
it'll be hard to win him to our side.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:26.200
After all, he has very noble blood.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:35.310
There's no such thing as noble blood.
Nor shitty blood, either.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:40.990
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:44.700
I'mma go take a shit.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.080
Asirpa-chan, no watching.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.420
What is it, Shiraishi?

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.050
Run away with me.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.150
This is our only chance.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:10.770
Nopperabo created a code with the tattoos that 
only his daughter can crack, right?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:14.460
Which means you have to know what it is.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:19.980
Maybe Kiroranke took you here because 
he's trying to make you remember.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.120
That's why I haven't said anything so far.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:27.030
But it's too dangerous to 
stay with him in Russia!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:31.180
And he was hiding things from us!

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:37.210
He and Wilk were trying to steal 
the Ainu gold to fight Russia!

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.720
We'll leave our stuff.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.540
We need to put as much distance between 
us and them as we can before they find out...

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:45.140
I'm staying.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.050
Why?

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:49.270
My old name was Yulbars.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.680
I was born as a Tatar,

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:54.100
but also carried the 
blood of a Karafuto Ainu.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.610
My great-grandmother was a Karafuto Ainu 
who was sold to the peoples of Tunguska

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:02.070
to pay off a debt, and taken to the Amur River.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.810
Wilk's father was also a Karafuto Ainu.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:13.250
The emperor we killed was the man who'd 
signed the Treaty of St. Petersburg.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:18.340
We fought for freedom for the 
ethnic minorities of the Far East.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:26.050
That includes my sons, Asirpa, 
and the Ainu of Hokkaido.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.190
I want to know more...

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.850
Who was my father? 
How did he become Nopperabo?

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:43.110
<i>And did he really leave behind 
a code only I can crack?</i>

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.520
<i>I need to know.</i>

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.000
<i>After all the killing is done, 
we'll find the gold, and then...</i>

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.660
<i>Will we kill more?</i>

00:12:56.320 --> 00:13:00.200
<i>Should it should be found?</i>

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.600
<i>Or should it be left in the darkness?</i>

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.400
Forward! Forward!

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.720
Run!

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.650
Come on, now's not the time to stop!

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:22.090
We're not getting hit, thanks to Yuusaku!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.330
Forward!

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:55.060
Private Ogata...

00:13:56.530 --> 00:14:01.270
Yuusaku-dono is, it seems, 
braver than I thought.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.110
He has a tight hold on everyone's hearts.

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:09.160
So I won't be killing him, then?

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.080
I understand.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.110
His fever's gone down.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:23.090
This headband is said to drive away 
sickness demons. It seems to work.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.690
Thank you.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:26.730
No, it's fine.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.090
You're giving this to me?

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:31.640
What is it?

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.430
This is for Ogata.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:36.130
It heals headaches when worn, they say.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:40.690
There are many different shapes 
for curing different things.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:45.180
They're willing to give you a 
charm shaped like a child's penis.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:52.370
How did you know that sometimes after 
I go to a brothel, my dick hurts?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.740
Because you have a disgusting face.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:55.950
How rude!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.700
Brother, what is it you 
wanted to talk to me about?

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.870
It's so late.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.520
If the captain finds us, we're in trouble.

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.850
This way, Yuusaku-dono.

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:31.400
Here.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:37.790
A prisoner?

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:40.660
Here? Why?

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:47.090
Yuusaku-dono, have you killed a 
single Russian since coming here?

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:52.290
True, a flag-bearer doesn't 
even carry a rifle.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.010
Their role is to charge into the front 
lines and inspire their fellows.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:00.090
But the other flag-bearers draw their swords.

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:03.130
Why don't you?

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.590
Because...

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:09.230
My first priority is to protect the 
flag that the emperor gave me.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.960
So you don't want to get your hands dirty,

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.780
and you're using your job as 
a flag-bearer as an excuse.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.910
No... that's not true!

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.850
Then kill him, please.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:22.790
Brother, he's a prisoner of war!

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.420
Do you intend to be the one 
person who's pure at the end of this war?

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.330
Yuusaku-dono, I want to see you kill him.

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:33.630
I can't!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.320
My father told me not to kill anyone, 
no matter what anybody else did.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:42.810
The flag is a holy thing 
to the soldiers around it,

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.420
and so its bearer has to be a 
virgin to uphold their superstition.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:50.600
And... while this isn't a military rule, 
and just my father's interpretation...

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.520
By refusing to kill the enemy, 
I'll be an object of worship

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:55.200
to the men around me, giving them courage!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:59.780
Because everyone feels guilt when killing!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.650
Guilt?

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:09.020
Guilt over the ones we killed?

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:13.410
Nobody feels that way.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.360
You're just saying that, right?

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:18.290
Everybody is like me. I know it.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.980
You're not that kind of person, brother!

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:27.790
Someday you'll understand...

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:34.160
That no one in the world should be able 
to kill and not feel any guilt over it!

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.600
Ogata, you awake?

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.400
What are you doing?

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:16.120
It's a reindeer shoulder blade.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:18.860
He's cleaning it by removing 
all the meat from it.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:22.120
He's going to tell our fortunes.

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:28.920
They burn bones in the fire, and use the 
cracks that appear to tell many things.

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:32.330
"Tomorrow, you'll catch a bear hunting."

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.920
"Tomorrow, you'll catch two reindeer hunting."

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.550
"You'll return home midway through hunting 
because you have something to do."

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:43.250
If the long line that forms, the "road,"
 burns with a black smudge,

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.350
it means the weather will turn bad.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.860
So what does it say?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.480
"People will come from behind."

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:56.120
That's not bad news, is it?

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:02.150
A bad sign looks like this, they say.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:07.640
I'm glad we didn't get a sign like that.

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.190
Thank you for lending us your reindeer.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:17.450
We'll give them to your brother in the north.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.650
Thank you.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.650
I apologize for the harm we caused you.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.780
It's fine, it's fine.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:29.890
Shiraishi Yoshitake, this is goodbye.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:35.150
You're right. I'm a wanted 
man here in Russia.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.720
If you stay with me, you'll be 
in greater danger than before.

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:43.450
You don't need to run away from me.

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:49.440
Hijikata Toshizou and Lieutenant Tsurumi 
both have a copy of your tattoos.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:51.790
There's no need to keep you here now.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:57.110
Yeah, gold won't do you 
much good if you're dead.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:00.630
Asirpa-chan's burden is a 
very different one than mine.

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:06.100
You've helped me with a lot.
 Thanks, Shiraishi.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.600
Stay safe! Don't get caught by any weirdos!

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.950
Now, then...

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:26.470
At times like this, you've gotta get smart.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:31.550
You need to take a broad view, and see who's 
going to survive the battle for the gold.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:36.780
Then you latch onto them like a flea on 
a horse and don't let go till payday.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.210
Got it?

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:44.930
Now, then, maybe I'll head back to 
Hokkaido and suck up to Lieutenant Tsurumi.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:21:01.900
If I stop running... Shiraishi, you take
 Asirpa-san to Abashiri Prison.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:05.910
Take care of her, Shiraishi!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.620
Wait!

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.620
Wait!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:16.930
It's Shiraishi!

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:23.170
What, did you change your mind?

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:30.920
I'm sure there are lots of places to have 
fun with hot blondes in Russia, right?

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:35.230
Shiraishi Yoshitake is a 
man with global tastes!

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:38.310
Go home!

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:43.610
Jeez... don't blame me if your 
dick starts to hurt again.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:47.260
Don't worry. I've got this.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Meko Oyashi</b>

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:39.350
Next Time: "Meko Oyashi."
